      "term": "Samir Loisir",
      "caseSensitive": true,
      "short": "A legendary Gurdi businessman who rose from the coal mines to fabulous wealth; Savoir Faire holds him up as proof that anyone can get rich.",
      "details": "Encyclopedia says he made his first millions selling the ultra-rare mineral phasium to the luxury jeweller Zachaël et Cie, and the rest through wise investments and the invention of pleochroic lights.\n\nSavoir Faire claims he grew up eating dirt in Gurdi's mines and still made fifty-five billion reál, so you have no excuses. Logic thinks both the fortune and the dirt-eating are exaggerated.",
      "seeAlso": [
