    {
      "id": "smallest-church-in-saint-saens",
      "term": "Smallest Church in Saint-Saëns",
      "aliases": [
        "The Smallest Church in Saint-Saëns",
        "The Smallest Church In Saint-Saëns"
      ],
      "caseSensitive": true,
      "short": "A slow, melancholy organ song about a tiny church by the sea; you can find it on tape and sing it at the Whirling-in-Rags karaoke.",
      "details": "The lyrics describe a tiny church in Saint-Saëns with an even tinier yard, the sea mist and pale cliffs, and they end on a note of loneliness. Garte recognises the song at once.\n\nA tape of it turns up in an abandoned summer house on the coast. You need a tape player or porta-reel to listen to it, and you can hand it to Garte if you want to perform it on the karaoke stage.",
      "spoiler": "It is the sad song you sang during your binge; Klaasje and Sylvie, the Whirling's former waitress, can both identify it. Egg Head turns it down as far too sad for his dance music.",
      "seeAlso": [
