    {
      "id": "son-of-lung",
      "term": "Son of Lung",
      "aliases": [
        "Far Out Son of Lung"
      ],
      "caseSensitive": true,
      "short": "A police urban legend about a detective so far undercover, or so far gone, that he forgets who he is. People compare you to him.",
      "details": "Kim calls it an urban myth about an officer who goes so deep undercover he can't remember his own identity. Another explanation is that it's a cultural reference to a detective who uses wildly experimental methods.\n\nA heckler in the Whirling-in-Rags mockingly calls you the 'Far Out Son of Lung': a supercop who drinks himself into delirium to solve crimes.",
      "inspiredBy": "The name echoes 'Far-Out Son of Lung and the Ramblings of a Madman', a 1995 track by the electronic group The Future Sound of London.",
