    {
      "id": "stained-glass-window",
      "term": "Stained Glass Window",
      "aliases": [
        "Shards of Dei"
      ],
      "caseSensitive": true,
      "short": "A cracked stained glass window in the abandoned Dolorian church showing Dolores Dei, the 'young mother of humanism', in apricot-coloured light.",
      "details": "The tall, sad figure is painted on a single pane, with a crack running across her body; cold air and snow get in through it. Visual Calculus can reconstruct the shattered part: once there was an older woman below her and a line of text. You can kneel before her, and Kim quietly draws an x-shaped cross from shoulder to shoulder.\n\nKim identifies the building as the Dolorian Church of Humanity, also called the Small Pinewood Church, the last of seven old stave churches on the coast.",
      "spoiler": "Kim suspects the church was shot up in a police raid some time ago, and that Precinct 41 was among the three precincts involved.",
      "seeAlso": [
