    {
      "id": "un-pays-infernal",
      "term": "Un Pays Infernal",
      "caseSensitive": true,
      "short": "A dense anti-capitalist book of critical theory; the student communist reading group in the apartment building has worked through it.",
      "details": "The title is French for 'An Infernal Country'. The reading group lists it among their past assignments and credits it to Abelard; another description names the author as Dr. Benoit Mejean, an angry humanities doctor at La Cherte University in Sur-La-Clef, who promises to cover everything wrong with capitalism once and for all.\n\nThe book jokes that the more communist books you read, the more communist your brain becomes, but in practice it reads as near-impenetrable jargon.",
      "seeAlso": [
