    {
      "id": "wholeness-unity-balance",
      "term": "Wholeness, Unity, Balance",
      "caseSensitive": true,
      "short": "A self-help health book by Matthias W. Dundas on the paranormal shelf of Plaisance's bookstore, claiming the mind can cure nearly anything.",
      "details": "Like many books on that shelf, it gives medical advice to people who can't afford doctors while dismissing real medicine. Its logic: if your mind has to heal you, it was your mind that made you ill. Chapters cover harvesting magnesium from plants, carrying on drinking with a ruined liver, and an old Seraise remedy using duck gall bladder. It is not worth buying.",
