    {
      "id": "wirral",
      "term": "Wirrâl",
      "caseSensitive": true,
      "short": "A hugely popular fantasy board game of maps, dice and miniatures, with welkin, dweorgr, faerie folk and pygmies; you can buy a module at the bookstore.",
      "details": "Its box promises an escape from modern life into a pastoral world of magic, monsters and dungeons, free of isolas, nations and technology. Players create heroes from five races (welkin, dweorgr, humans, faerie folk and pygmies), read an intricate rulebook and roll dice. The setting is known for its complicated system of political alignments, though most players just hack through dungeons for loot.\n\nPlaisance sells a Third Edition module at her bookstore. Inside are a map, a booklet, a 24-sided die and a little plastic figurine of a communard, which clearly doesn't belong to the game.",
      "inspiredBy": "Dungeons & Dragons and similar Tolkien-style fantasy games (the welkin and dweorgr are its elves and dwarves).",
      "seeAlso": [
