      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "wirral-untethered",
      "term": "Wirrâl Untethered",
      "caseSensitive": true,
      "short": "An ambitious radio game set in a version of the Wirrâl world, developed by Fortress Accident, a failed studio in the Doomed Commercial Area.",
      "details": "The idea was an automated role-playing game run on radiocomputers: players anywhere could join through call-in stations with two-way radios, while a game master frequency coordinated the stories. Its world was a modified Wirrâl with heat death thrown in.\n\nThe studio had 18 staff and tried to make a 4,000,000 reál game with 400,000 in the bank. The Novelty Dicemaker sells a special die for it, decorated with motifs of ice, death and loss.",
      "spoiler": "The game was lost: an unexplained numeric anomaly struck just as the project was being compiled, and it came back completely blank.",
      "seeAlso": [
